1
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
The new morning we've finally found

2
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
is being hampered by the past.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

6
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
but the past so full of remorse.

8
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

9
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

10
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

11
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

12
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

13
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
It's about now that a teardrop

14
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

15
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

16
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

17
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Will this rain ever stop?

18
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

19
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
I've been freezing for a long time.

20
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

21
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

22
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

23
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

24
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
Tsutsumarete iikana

25
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Today, the rain falls again;

26
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

27
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

28
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

29
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

30
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

31
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

32
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

33
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:39,820
Huh?

34
00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:43,330
That's strange, I could have sworn it was this way...

35
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,450
No, was it that way?

36
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:47,460
Are you lost, Fullmetal?

37
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:49,670
Shut up!

38
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:53,460
We're lost because we came back to make sure that a certain incompetent moron wasn't doing anything dumb!

39
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:56,840
No one asked you to do it.

40
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:58,590
I'm surprised you can say that!

41
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:00,050
If Scar and I hadn't been there,

42
00:02:00,050 --> 00:02:02,720
you definitely would have fallen from the right path!

43
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:04,640
Quit demanding my gratitude.

44
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:08,020
It's thanks to the Lieutenant that I was able to stop myself.

45
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:09,480
What did you say?!

46
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:12,980
They're so loud. We're going to be found by the enemy.

47
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:19,360
Scar, I'm going to go ahead and thank you while I still can.

48
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:21,910
For convincing the Colonel.

49
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:31,710
Although it would probably just anger you Ishbalans if you were to be thanked by someone like myself.

50
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:36,710
I think he was able...

51
00:02:38,090 --> 00:02:39,550
...to return to his old self.

52
00:02:47,390 --> 00:02:48,390
Thank you.

53
00:02:54,110 --> 00:02:56,150
No need to thank me...

54
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:03,420
The Adults' Way of Life

55
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:03,420
The Adults' Way of Life

56
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,660
Okay, roger!

57
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,330
Understood!

58
00:03:10,330 --> 00:03:12,830
Hey! You can stop firing now!

59
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:13,750
Cease fire!

60
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,630
A message to the soldiers of the Central Army.

61
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:21,550
A message to the soldiers of the Central Army.

62
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:24,970
We, the Briggs forces, have occupied mission headquarters.

63
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,180
Damn those traitors...!

64
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:28,770
We are currently holding thirteen hostages, including Brigadier General Clemin.

65
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:30,230
I repeat.

66
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:34,230
We, the Briggs forces, have occupied mission headquarters.

67
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:37,770
We demand that the soldiers of the Central Army cease fire immediately.

68
00:03:38,230 --> 00:03:41,360
We are currently holding Brigadier General Clemin hostage.

69
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:47,870
So the reason why you were going all flashy with the tanks was to mask the noise of the tunnel digging!

70
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:51,120
That's right.

71
00:03:55,630 --> 00:03:56,840
What was that?!

72
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:58,210
I couldn't hear!

73
00:03:59,170 --> 00:04:00,000
What?!

74
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,210
Is this true?!

75
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:02,340
What's the matter?

76
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:05,390
Mission headquarters has fallen to the Briggs soldiers!

77
00:04:05,390 --> 00:04:07,680
Brigadier General Clemin has been taken hostage!

78
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:10,310
Mission headquarters!

79
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:11,680
Is Buccaneer there?

80
00:04:12,350 --> 00:04:13,140
Captain!

81
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:18,440
There are a great number of these one-eyed blue humanoid monsters.

82
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:22,070
It takes a lot to kill them, and they also eat humans!

83
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:25,700
No matter what happens, keep all the gates closed!

84
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:28,830
You mustn't let a single one of them out into the city!

85
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:32,290
Annihilate them within the headquarters grounds!

86
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:36,210
Aye, ma'am!

87
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:40,800
What the hell is Clemin doing?

88
00:04:41,550 --> 00:04:43,670
From here on out, I'll take charge!

89
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:47,180
This will be the new mission headquarters!

90
00:04:54,350 --> 00:04:56,520
The Führer President's chair...

91
00:04:57,850 --> 00:05:00,940
If we overcome this crisis, it'll be mine!

92
00:05:13,790 --> 00:05:16,290
Still more of them?!

93
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:23,590
M-Major General, what the hell are these things?!

94
00:05:24,170 --> 00:05:26,510
An immortal army, apparently.

95
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:30,050
They're soldiers that don't fear death,

96
00:05:30,050 --> 00:05:32,600
made by affixing human souls onto dolls.

97
00:05:33,930 --> 00:05:37,350
You soldiers will someday be turned into those.

98
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:49,700
That thing's still going to move?!

99
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:51,620
How much does it take to kill it for good?

100
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:53,740
Then here I go again!

101
00:06:01,790 --> 00:06:03,630
What tenacity...!

102
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:05,920
Oh no!

103
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:13,470
Major!

104
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,760
Major General Armstrong!

105
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:17,390
Don't come!

106
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:20,270
It's after us only!

107
00:06:20,270 --> 00:06:21,520
Stay away!

108
00:06:30,450 --> 00:06:32,120
So stubborn.

109
00:06:32,570 --> 00:06:35,660
I'm going to kill the female general!

110
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,210
Pull!

111
00:06:51,890 --> 00:06:53,850
Keep it up!

112
00:06:57,770 --> 00:07:00,480
Please, you two! Run away while you can!

113
00:07:02,810 --> 00:07:03,940
This way! Hurry!

114
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,820
Now, Major!

115
00:07:07,070 --> 00:07:09,400
Are you asking me to run...?

116
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:15,910
Are you asking me to run from the battlefield again?!

117
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:20,080
There's no way I could!

118
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:50,780
I like that resolve not to run.

119
00:07:51,950 --> 00:07:53,490
You're quite handsome.

120
00:07:53,950 --> 00:07:58,120
Well, not nearly as handsome as my husband, though.

121
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:01,910
Who are you?

122
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:05,170
Ah, the female officer.

123
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:08,540
Which means you must be Major General Armstrong.

124
00:08:09,090 --> 00:08:13,420
Your subordinate with the mohawk asked me to come help you guys.

125
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:17,800
That was unnecessary of him...

126
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:21,430
This is such a drag...

127
00:08:32,530 --> 00:08:34,200
Here he comes, Dear!

128
00:08:34,570 --> 00:08:35,700
Gotcha!

129
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:50,130
Who might that gentleman be?

130
00:08:50,130 --> 00:08:51,380
My husband.

131
00:09:10,190 --> 00:09:14,190
Courage increased by hundred-fold, 
muscles increased by thousand-fold!

132
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,560
Ouch...

133
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:00,740
He can still move?!

134
00:10:11,630 --> 00:10:14,500
Am I... going to die?

135
00:10:15,170 --> 00:10:16,300
Die...?

136
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:19,680
What does it mean... to die?

137
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:24,470
It's too much of a drag... to think.

138
00:10:25,350 --> 00:10:27,350
Even living...

139
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:31,810
...is a drag...

140
00:10:43,530 --> 00:10:44,490
Major!

141
00:10:43,950 --> 00:10:44,780
Major!

142
00:10:56,710 --> 00:10:59,260
All that's left are the skinny small fries!

143
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:01,510
Annihilate them with everything you've got!

144
00:11:01,510 --> 00:11:02,220
Roger!

145
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,390
Sorry, I need to take a quick break.

146
00:11:10,390 --> 00:11:11,440
Yes, ma'am!

147
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,850
Please leave the rest to us!

148
00:11:16,190 --> 00:11:19,940
I don't know who you are,
but I very much appreciate your help.

149
00:11:20,490 --> 00:11:21,860
You're welcome.

150
00:11:22,990 --> 00:11:25,870
I assume you must be a famous martial artist.

151
00:11:26,370 --> 00:11:27,290
Me?

152
00:11:27,870 --> 00:11:30,450
No, no, I'm a housewife and an alchemist.

153
00:11:30,830 --> 00:11:33,170
You've heard of the Elric Brothers, right?

154
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:35,630
I'm like a relative of theirs.

155
00:11:35,630 --> 00:11:38,500
So you're Izumi Curtis?

156
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:40,420
Yup.

157
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:42,380
Are the Elric Brothers also here?

158
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,970
Yes, they should be.

159
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:56,560
Well then, I guess we should
take care of the rest of the dolls.

160
00:11:57,110 --> 00:11:59,190
Can you stand, Sister?

161
00:11:59,190 --> 00:12:00,940
This is nothing.

162
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:04,950
Hey hey, rest up a bit! You're heavily wounded.

163
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:13,120
Us adults can't just lie around while the young ones are fighting.

164
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:19,130
We have to show the young ones, the ones who will carry this world from now on,

165
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:22,470
the way we adults, the ones who currently carry this world, live our lives.

166
00:12:25,930 --> 00:12:28,430
Then I guess we'll help out too!

167
00:12:28,430 --> 00:12:30,180
That'll be wonderful!

168
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:32,640
Having you two on our side is equivalent to gaining one hundred men.

169
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:37,190
Nah... don't expect too much out of us.

170
00:12:37,730 --> 00:12:41,030
I'm apparently a "human sacrifice" or something,

171
00:12:41,650 --> 00:12:45,110
so I'm going to be getting out of here after I fight for a bit.

172
00:12:45,990 --> 00:12:48,160
Before I get captured by someone really dangerous.

173
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:06,090
You're being so sullen even though we're in the middle of a heartfelt reunion?

174
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:13,100
You've gotten really boring.

175
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:18,850
You used to be pretty fun, with all those emotions.

176
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:29,950
Lust, greed, sloth, gluttony, envy, wrath, and pride.

177
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:33,290
They say that man has seven sins.

178
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:37,710
Too much greed would certainly destroy one's self,

179
00:13:37,710 --> 00:13:44,550
but on the other hand, all of those emotions are absolutely necessary to understand other humans.

180
00:13:45,510 --> 00:13:47,300
Why did you let go of them?

181
00:13:56,930 --> 00:13:59,190
Geez, that was dangerous.

182
00:14:09,490 --> 00:14:11,490
Listen to what I have to say!

183
00:14:13,330 --> 00:14:14,580
You're kidding me!

184
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:23,040
Cut it out, man.

185
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:25,840
I'm not too good at fighting.

186
00:14:47,530 --> 00:14:48,690
Answer me!

187
00:14:48,690 --> 00:14:53,320
Why did you create the homunculi, keep them by your side, and have them call you 'Father'?!

188
00:14:56,660 --> 00:14:59,210
Back when you were in the flask,

189
00:14:59,210 --> 00:15:02,790
you used to even make fun of the community known as a family!

190
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:11,340
Could it be that you actually wanted a family like other humans have?

191
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:30,860
Where did he go?

192
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:34,910
Don't tell me he's going to hide until the 
Nationwide Transmutation Circle activates?

193
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:45,960
It's not that I want to become human.

194
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:49,760
I want to become a perfect being.

195
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:54,840
I'm going to be taking...

196
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,470
...the philosopher's stone that's inside of you.

197
00:16:14,490 --> 00:16:17,320
Finally, your expression changed.

198
00:16:19,830 --> 00:16:21,540
What did you do?

199
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:25,170
Something you didn't do.

200
00:16:27,380 --> 00:16:29,250
You probably won't understand.

201
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:33,760
You threw away something important along with your emotions.

202
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:35,890
Something important?

203
00:16:37,510 --> 00:16:42,520
Don't even think you'll be able to defeat us easily.

204
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:47,770
God dammit!

205
00:16:47,940 --> 00:16:49,440
This won't do.

206
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:52,150
The tire is completely stuck.

207
00:16:52,150 --> 00:16:54,360
Look what you did, mustache boy!

208
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:56,700
The solar eclipse will begin if we take our time like this!

209
00:16:56,910 --> 00:16:58,320
Shut up!

210
00:16:58,320 --> 00:17:00,450
Hurry up and pull the car out!

211
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:02,200
Oh boy...

212
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:08,420
Doctor Marcoh, please back away.

213
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:11,210
Mr. Heinkel and I can handle it.

214
00:17:11,210 --> 00:17:13,130
No, but...

215
00:17:13,130 --> 00:17:15,260
It'll be fine. Just leave it to us.

216
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,680
Okay, here we go!

217
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:20,850
One, two, three!

218
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:34,240
Go surrender to the mission headquarters.

219
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:35,530
Hurry up and go.

220
00:17:35,530 --> 00:17:36,700
Yes, sir!

221
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:38,070
Thank you very much!

222
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:45,160
Well, thanks to the dolls getting rid of so many central soldiers,

223
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,830
gaining full control of the place is a piece of cake.

224
00:17:56,510 --> 00:17:59,510
We're going to keep up this pace and gain control of the main gate.

225
00:17:59,510 --> 00:18:00,680
Aye, sir!

226
00:18:11,060 --> 00:18:13,860
Looks like there's not much for us to do...

227
00:18:16,690 --> 00:18:17,860
You!

228
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:19,030
Damn you!

229
00:18:19,030 --> 00:18:20,240
Why?!

230
00:18:20,990 --> 00:18:25,580
Weren't you made to listen to our orders?!

231
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:29,040
Was that man lying to us?!

232
00:18:30,540 --> 00:18:32,540
S-Stay away!

233
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:36,710
I wasn't meant to die here!

234
00:18:52,610 --> 00:18:55,400
I don't know who you are, but good work.

235
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,360
Be my bodyguard.

236
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:59,320
If you do, I'll specially-

237
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:08,000
Mind telling us about "that man" whom you speak of?

238
00:19:19,630 --> 00:19:21,470
This is gruesome.

239
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,060
Will you take command from here?

240
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:36,020
I don't understand how someone could sit in a place where they'd make such an easy target for a sniper.

241
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:37,270
Let's go.

242
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:39,440
Roger!

243
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:40,860
Sister.

244
00:19:44,490 --> 00:19:46,280
Where does this passage lead to?

245
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:48,580
Seems like it goes down pretty deep.

246
00:19:51,790 --> 00:19:55,130
Could it be the hole which the dolls came out of?

247
00:19:55,130 --> 00:19:58,380
If so, it could lead underground.

248
00:19:58,380 --> 00:19:59,420
Yes.

249
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:01,670
Okay, understood.

250
00:20:02,090 --> 00:20:03,090
Madam!

251
00:20:03,090 --> 00:20:05,970
Buccaneer and his men have captured the main gate.

252
00:20:06,390 --> 00:20:09,310
There was little resistance, and they sustained only minor damage.

253
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:11,430
The entrance to the main gate has also been seized.

254
00:20:11,430 --> 00:20:14,560
They've stationed the tanks there and are using it as a primary defensive position.

255
00:20:15,810 --> 00:20:18,520
The Buccaneer squadron shall stay on stand-by.

256
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:25,320
Please be sure not to open the gate until every single one of the dolls have been exterminated.

257
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:26,820
Roger that.

258
00:20:27,410 --> 00:20:28,620
This is the west gate.

259
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:30,990
We, the white squadron from Briggs, have taken control of the place.

260
00:20:30,990 --> 00:20:32,250
This is the north gate.

261
00:20:32,250 --> 00:20:34,120
Black squadron, taken control!

262
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:36,250
Blue squadron, taken control of the east gate.

263
00:20:36,250 --> 00:20:38,710
Yellow squadron, we've seized their arsenal!

264
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:42,720
It's just as you hear, Major General Armstrong!

265
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:46,970
The Briggs Army has gained control of 90% of Central Headquarters.

266
00:20:48,010 --> 00:20:50,510
Victory is ours.

267
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:57,980
We won!!

268
00:21:08,450 --> 00:21:11,200
Looks like the Colonel didn't make it in time.

269
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:13,410
Hip hip, hooray!

270
00:21:13,580 --> 00:21:15,870
Hip hip, hooray!

271
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,290
Hip hip, hooray!

272
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:20,840
Hip hip, hooray!

273
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:23,300
Hip hip, hooray!

274
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:24,670
Did you miss me?

275
00:21:28,180 --> 00:21:33,680
Seems like you guys started a party while I was away.

276
00:21:34,350 --> 00:21:39,440
From here on out, I myself will take command and annihilate the traitors.

277
00:21:40,060 --> 00:21:43,730
I order all unengaged central soldiers to lend me a hand.

278
00:21:44,860 --> 00:21:47,570
King... Bradley...?!

279
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:50,780
So he was alive.

280
00:21:51,370 --> 00:21:52,240
Where?!

281
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:53,830
Where will he attack from?!

282
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:08,300
Salute the Führer President!

283
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:42,800
Ever since that day passed,

284
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:42,800
Ano hi kara zutto

285
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:47,050
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

286
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:47,050
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

287
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:52,600
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

288
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:52,600
Itami wo kasanetemo

289
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,710
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

290
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,710
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

291
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,150
I'll never be able

292
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,150
Mou modorenai

293
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,650
to return to those days.

294
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,650
Ikutsumo no hibi

295
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:08,740
I'm still powerless.

296
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:08,740
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

297
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,990
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

298
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,990
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

299
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:19,860
memories of when you were still with me.

300
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:19,860
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

301
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,880
I long to become

302
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,880
Kyou yori motto

303
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,630
stronger than I am now,

304
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,630
Tsuyoku naritai

305
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:30,770
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

306
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:30,770
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

307
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,140
If the wind happens to stop

308
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,140
Arukitsuzukete

309
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:35,850
in the midst of my long journey,

310
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:35,850
Kaze ga yandara

311
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:40,560
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

312
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:40,560
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

313
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:47,900
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

314
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:47,900
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

315
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:53,450
A rainbow spans across the sky.

316
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:53,450
Niji ga kakaruyo

317
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:03,580
The king's sword brings about destruction, death,

318
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:05,750
waste, and despair.

319
00:24:06,210 --> 00:24:11,130
He devastates all that stands in his way with unmatched power.

320
00:24:12,670 --> 00:24:17,140
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

321
00:24:17,140 --> 00:24:21,660
Episode 56, The Return of the Führer

322
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:21,660
The Return of the Führer

323
00:24:23,270 --> 00:24:27,650
His home is the battlefield.
